			note = "{npc:14722} takes cloth for {faction:72}. The arrow leads to him; he stands upstairs inside his building. Each first donation of 60 Wool, Silk, Mageweave and {item:14047} pays 150 reputation once; after the {item:14047} one, {quest:7796} pays 50 for every 20 {item:14047}, as often as you like. The Auction House is the quickest source of cloth. In Classic, quests pay full reputation while they are at most 5 levels below you, so do Elwynn (levels 1-10), {zone:1436} (10-18), Redridge (15-25) and {zone:1431} (20-30) while you level through them. After the donations come the level 52-58 quests of the {zone:1422} and the {zone:1428} (about 1,150), then the optional low-level hubs, best rate first: Northshire and the city errands (about 40 a minute at full value), the {area:717} (30), Eastvale and {area:87} (25). Every {faction:72} gain also gives a quarter as much to {zone:1455}, {zone:1457} and the Gnomeregan Exiles, except quests in the level 1-10 start areas. Legacy Diplomat adds up to 10% to every gain.",
